{
  "title": "Window Swing Total",
  "description": "## Task\n\nA sensor logs one reading per minute. For every run of exactly `k` consecutive readings, the swing of that run is its largest reading minus its smallest reading. Return the total of the swings over all such runs, taken from the first run to the last.\n\n## Input\n\n- `readings` — a non-empty list of integers.\n- `k` — the run length, between 1 and the number of readings.\n\n## Output\n\nA single integer: the sum of (max - min) over every run of `k` consecutive readings.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nwindow_swing_total([1, 3, 2, 5, 4], 3)  # returns 8\nwindow_swing_total([4, 4, 4], 2)  # returns 0\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 ≤ length of `readings` ≤ 10^5\n- -10^9 ≤ each reading ≤ 10^9\n- 1 ≤ `k` ≤ length of `readings`\n- Expect large inputs where recomputing each run from scratch is too slow.\n",
  "signature": "def window_swing_total(readings: list[int], k: int) -> int",
  "topic": "monotonic deque",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "category": "stacks-queues",
